# SHA-256 of every upstream file this repository carries from LMDB LMDB_1.0.1
# (tag LMDB_1.0.1, commit 6f0a32496a5aadee15a5e5103c479bd3355ae273,
# https://github.com/LMDB/lmdb), plus the one independent fixture this
# package's tests read.
#
# 43 records, 689093 bytes, in three groups:
#
#   42 files   the whole of libraries/liblmdb/, upstream's own liblmdb
#              directory as imported at that commit. That is the C library
#              core (mdb.c, midl.c, module.c), the reference tool this
#              package's interoperability gate builds (mdb_dump.c), the two
#              headers those units include by name (lmdb.h, midl.h), the
#              other three upstream tools (mdb_stat, mdb_copy, mdb_load,
#              mdb_drop), upstream's own test programs and sample databases
#              (mtest.c..mtest6.c, mtest_enc.c, mtest_enc2..4.c,
#              mtest_remap.c, mplay.c, chacha8.c/h, crypto.c, cryptoc.c,
#              sample-mdb.txt, sample-bdb.txt), the five man pages, the
#              licence and copyright files, and the Makefile, Doxyfile,
#              CHANGES, intro.doc, upgrading.doc, tooltag and upstream's own
#              libraries/liblmdb/.gitignore. It is a complete copy of that one
#              directory, not a copy of the upstream repository: upstream also
#              ships contrib/, the OpenLDAP tree it lives in, its own CI and
#              its documentation site, none of which is here.
#
#    1 file    testdata/corpus.txt, the known-answer corpus. Not upstream's
#              and not compiled: `tests.zig` embeds it with @embedFile and
#              `testdata/interop.zig` writes it through the facade and
#              compares upstream's `mdb_dump -p` output against it. It is
#              hashed here because a silent edit to it moves every published
#              expectation in the package at once.
#
# The package ships the complete libraries/liblmdb directory, not only the
# translation units compiled into the archive. All 42 upstream records and
# the independent corpus below survive materialization from `.paths`.
# Run `sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256` from either repository or package root;
# every listed file must exist and match. Missing files are not expected.
#
# Deliberately absent, each for a stated reason:
#   build.zig, build.zig.zon, translate.h, zig/, tests.zig, smoke.zig,
#   cross-test.profile.sh, testdata/interop.zig, consumer/,
#   .github/workflows/verify.yml, .gitignore and this fork's six documents --
#   this fork's own files, listed in NOTICE.md. The package-root `.gitignore`
#   is a fork file that keeps upstream's rules and appends Zig entries;
#   `libraries/liblmdb/.gitignore` is upstream's and IS hashed above.
#   .zig-cache/ and zig-out/ -- build output, ignored by the fork's
#   `.gitignore` and absent from `.paths`.
#   UPSTREAM.sha256 itself -- a record cannot contain its own digest.
#
# These are the bytes in this working tree, hashed as a raw byte read (Bun
# `Bun.file(path).arrayBuffer()`, SHA-256 from `node:crypto`) on 2026-10-01.
# No shell hashing command and no git command produced any line of this file.
# They are not a signature and not a Git object id: see UPSTREAM.md,
# "Integrity", for what they do and do not establish, and for how the
# whole-tree archive receipt is a different record from this per-file one.
#
# Verify with:  sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256
